sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-model-fidelity> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "@drmichaellevin 8-law mathematical synthesis & biological-law-criteria suite — Model fidelity to source: 78/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-24"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Verified by running: Law 1's Hill fit is implemented (L213-L216) and reproduced (bounded 1-D minimiser gives G_eff 2.2600, RMS 3.0478; unfitted RMS 55.1846) (+2 restored); the Law 4 criteria-doc value now matches the code (+2 restored); the Law 6 docstring (L469-L477) is the implemented ODE with its actual results and the header no longer promises plasticity or extinction (+3 restored); `hill_curve` is consumed by the RMS (+1 restored). New deduction: the fit exposes that the Hill form the Lean theorem formalises (L30-L60) is the wrong function for the model the law is scored on - the BVP reach grows as G^0.48 with no plateau, the fitted half-saturation 2.26 lies outside the swept range [0, 2], the maximum deviation is 5.6 cells, and the assertion at L850 (fitted RMS < unfitted RMS) holds for any least-squares fit (-2). Unchanged deductions: Law 2's I_ion is an invented cubic and the wound is a hard clamp (-4); Law 8's k >= 17 threshold applies the square-lattice fraction to non-square k and pi_D is the builder's construction (-4); Law 5 is a 4-row truth table (-3); Law 2's and Law 7's Lean theorems state much less than their names claim (-2); panel A's new top axis (L616-L618) is labelled G_gj 0..2.0 but the curve is still drawn at g * 9.5 on the cell-index axis (L619), misaligning the ticks by ~0.09 G units (-1)." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py L239–L285: Law 2 unchanged since Pass 3: 20-cell ODE, cubic I_ion with roots -60 / -38 / -10 mV (L252-L253), hard clamp of cells 0-4 (never integrated, L260); gated tail -60.003 mV vs ohmic -10.0 mV (reproduced). Genuine two-regime dynamics on an invented current; no Cervera 2020 channel model or parameter set <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987ff10/models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py#L239-L285>",
            "models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py L323–L325: Law 3 G_gj sweep: G_gj multiplies every entry of Q (L309-L310), so the nullspace ratio is invariant by linear algebra; spread 1e-12 is guaranteed, not a result about electrodiffusion. Physically the invariance holds only in the zero-flux limit; with production / decay (as in BETSE) the ratio depends on permeability <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987ff10/models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py#L323-L325>",
            "models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py L421–L426: Law 5: the same 4-row x 3-gate truth table as v2 and Pass 3. The underlying fact - every symmetric Boolean function of (a, b) factors through a + b - is elementary <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987ff10/models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py#L421-L426>",
            "models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py L558–L568: Law 8 unchanged: thresholds k = 4, 16, 17 from applying 1 - 1/sqrt(k) to all k = 1..36; k = 17 is not realised by any m x m cluster (first exact square with strict dominance is k = 25, now stated in docs L66 and YAML L148); pi_D = b / sqrt(k) is the builder's construction <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987ff10/models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py#L558-L568>",
            "models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py L616–L620: Panel A: a twiny axis with xlim (0, 2) and the label 'Law 1 Conductance G_gj (0..2.0)' was added (L616-L618), but the reach curve is still plotted at g_grid * 9.5 on the Law 2 axis whose limits are (-0.95, 19.95) (L619-L620); G = 2 sits at 95.5 % of the width while the top-axis tick '2.0' sits at 100 %. Partial fix of the Pass 3.1 finding <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987ff10/models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py#L616-L620>",
            "models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py L850–L850: `assert hill_fitted_rms < hill_unfitted_rms`: true of any least-squares fit against a fixed parameter, so it cannot fail. Referee: the BVP reach over G in (0, 2] has log-log slope 0.48 and reaches 44.19 at G = 2 with no saturation; the fitted Hill plateau is N = 100 and its half-saturation 2.26 is outside the sweep; max |Hill_fit - PDE| = 5.6 cells. The Hill form is a mis-specified model of the BVP <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987ff10/models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py#L850-L850>",
            "morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_levin_youtube_channel_math.lean L235–L250: Law 7 theorem: integer telescoping and 0 < (e - f) - (a - b) ↔ a - b < e - f for all Int; no reference to a TPM, determinism or degeneracy; unchanged <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987ff10/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_levin_youtube_channel_math.lean#L235-L250>",
            "morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_levin_youtube_channel_math.lean L30–L60: Law 1 theorem is about tame_goal_radius_num = r (G + G_half) + r (N - 1) G - the numerator of the Hill form 1 + (N - 1) G/(G + G_half) - and proves collapse at G = 0, linear-in-N scaling at G_half = 0 and monotonicity in G. The Python metric (L728) is the BVP reach, which is not linear in N (continuum sqrt(G/k) tanh(N sqrt(k/G)) saturates in N). YAML L13 states the BVP formula while L17-L24 shows the Hill numerator: the formal and numerical artefacts of Law 1 are about different functions <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987ff10/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_levin_youtube_channel_math.lean#L30-L60>",
            "morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_levin_youtube_channel_math.lean L71–L97: Law 2 theorem named 'wound_isolation' proves symmetry/monotonicity of (1 + b_i)(1 + b_j) and antisymmetry of g (v_j - v_i). No bistability, isolation or ODE property is stated; unchanged since Pass 3 <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987ff10/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_levin_youtube_channel_math.lean#L71-L97>" ;
        pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-model-fidelity-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-model-fidelity-10>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-model-fidelity-11>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-model-fidelity-12>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-model-fidelity-13>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-model-fidelity-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-model-fidelity-3>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-model-fidelity-4>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-model-fidelity-5>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-model-fidelity-6>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-model-fidelity-7>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-model-fidelity-8>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-model-fidelity-9> ;
        pk:hasScore "0.78"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-model-fidelity-1> a pk:EvidenceItem ;
        rdfs:label "models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py L177–L233" ;
        dct:description "Law 1: 100-cell BVP, reach 32.0099 at G_gj = 1.0, 1.0 at G_gj = 0, 22.8602 at 0.5; continuum sqrt(1/k) tanh(N sqrt(k)) = 31.5097 (reproduced). Metric L728 and assertions L848-L849 use the BVP" ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987ff10/models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py#L177-L233> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-model-fidelity-10> a pk:EvidenceItem ;
        rdfs:label "models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py L570–L574" ;
        dct:description "Law 8 exact m x m directed bond count 4m^2 total, 4m perimeter, f_int = 1 - 1/m for m = 1..6 (re-derived; m = 5 gives 0.8)" ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987ff10/models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py#L570-L574> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-model-fidelity-11> a pk:EvidenceItem ;
        rdfs:label "morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_levin_youtube_channel_math.lean L107–L127" ;
        dct:description "Law 3 theorem: for all g ≠ 0, grad_ln_c, z_dV : Int, g (grad_ln_c + z_dV) = 0 ↔ grad_ln_c = -z_dV. Universally quantified, hypothesis used non-trivially; still the strongest statement in the file" ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987ff10/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_levin_youtube_channel_math.lean#L107-L127> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-model-fidelity-12> a pk:EvidenceItem ;
        rdfs:label "morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_levin_youtube_channel_math.lean L137–L157" ;
        dct:description "Law 4 theorem: p_sym r_sym = p_bulk r_bulk ∧ 0 < p_bulk ∧ r_sym < r_bulk → p_bulk < p_sym. Quantified and correct; h_flux assumes the law, so it proves a consequence of the law, not the law" ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987ff10/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_levin_youtube_channel_math.lean#L137-L157> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-model-fidelity-13> a pk:EvidenceItem ;
        rdfs:label "models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py L647–L647" ;
        dct:description "Panel C dashed curve labelled 'Analytic r_exit^-1 / Z (slope = -1.000)'; the nullspace values are the markers" ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987ff10/models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py#L647-L647> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-model-fidelity-2> a pk:EvidenceItem ;
        rdfs:label "models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py L211–L216" ;
        dct:description "Hill form fitted to pde_reach_curve by scipy.optimize.curve_fit with p0 = 1, bounds (1e-6, 1e4): G_eff 2.26, fitted RMS 3.0478 vs unfitted 55.1846 (reproduced independently with scipy.optimize.minimize_scalar, bounded: 2.2600 / 3.0478). Closes Pass 3.1 R2's unimplemented-fit finding; header L12-L14 now says 51 values and names curve_fit" ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987ff10/models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py#L211-L216> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-model-fidelity-3> a pk:EvidenceItem ;
        rdfs:label "models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py L368–L373" ;
        dct:description "Law 4 K_trap: row-normalised weights linspace(0.1, 2.5)^2.5 with the diagonal zeroed; column sums are not 1 (re-derived: 0.15..1.9), so the embedded chain is non-uniform and p ∝ 1/r can fail" ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987ff10/models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py#L368-L373> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-model-fidelity-4> a pk:EvidenceItem ;
        rdfs:label "models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py L375–L398" ;
        dct:description "Law 4 solve_stationary: rate_i = r_exit[i]^gamma at every alpha (L380), fit against log r_exit (L392). Slopes -1.0000 / -0.5598 / +0.1866 (r = 0.2866) at alpha = 0 / 0.5 / 0.9 (reproduced); the header (L23-L26) now says alpha in [0, 0.90]" ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987ff10/models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py#L375-L398> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-model-fidelity-5> a pk:EvidenceItem ;
        rdfs:label "docs/BIOLOGICAL_LAW_CRITERIA.md L62–L62" ;
        dct:description "Law 4 row: 'unconfounded C4 breakdown at alpha = 0.90 -> +0.1866' - now the value the code produces (summary JSON, --self-test, YAML L74, KG). Closes Pass 3.1 R1 for Law 4" ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987ff10/docs/BIOLOGICAL_LAW_CRITERIA.md#L62-L62> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-model-fidelity-6> a pk:EvidenceItem ;
        rdfs:label "models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py L300–L317" ;
        dct:description "Law 3 central-difference edge coefficients a_i = G(-1 + dv/2), b_{i+1} = G(1 + dv/2) (L309-L310): the per-edge ratio is the Pade(1,1) approximant of exp(-dv), so agreement with the Boltzmann ratio is a convergence result. Errors 0.007422, 0.001726, 0.000417, 0.000102, 2.5e-5 for N = 15..240 (reproduced; ratios 4.30, 4.14, 4.09, 4.08 = O(h^2))" ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987ff10/models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py#L300-L317> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-model-fidelity-7> a pk:EvidenceItem ;
        rdfs:label "models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py L469–L477" ;
        dct:description "Law 6 docstring now gives dx_M = -0.02 x_M + 0.25 sigma(12 (x_CS x_US - 0.50)), dx_US = -x_US + sigma(12 (I_US + 0.90 x_M x_CS - 0.55)) and results 0.0015 -> 1.0000, which is what L514-L522 implement and what the run returns. Closes Pass 3.1 R1 for Law 6" ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987ff10/models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py#L469-L477> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-model-fidelity-8> a pk:EvidenceItem ;
        rdfs:label "models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py L514–L535" ;
        dct:description "Law 6 3-node ODE [x_CS, x_M, x_US]: memory node decays at 0.02 and is charged only by x_CS * x_US; four phases (CS test, paired training t = 25, washout t = 5, CS test t = 10). CS-only US response 0.0015 -> 1.0, memory 4.7103 after training (reproduced). A hand-tuned minimal circuit, not a model from Pigozzi 2025 or Biswas 2023 - the docstring now says 'Pigozzi / Biswas 3-gene' only as attribution of the idea" ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987ff10/models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py#L514-L535> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-model-fidelity-9> a pk:EvidenceItem ;
        rdfs:label "models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py L511–L511" ;
        dct:description "Delta E = -eta N^2 is returned as `single_epoch_delta_e_identity` and asserted as a parameterised identity (L859)" ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987ff10/models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py#L511-L511> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic; independent cross-provider MorphoEval referee, Pass 3 / 3.1 / 3.2)" ;
        dct:identifier "claude-fable-5-1" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> ;
        foaf:homepage <https://www.anthropic.com> .
}

